# Elite DocCon Suite

Desktop transmittal workstation in the same family as Elite Databook Engine. Jira is the drawing register. DocCon matches issued PDFs, builds the transmittal log, sends (later), and writes the audit trail. A person still confirms before anything leaves.

## Working mode

- Planning and discussion until the user explicitly asks to code or to change files.
- Do not replace Jira. Do not scrape the Jira UI. Do not auto-send mail.
- Do not put API tokens, passwords, or `.env` secrets in this folder or anywhere on Dropbox. Operators enter/replace the Jira token in DocCon Settings; it is stored in Windows Credential Manager.
- Reuse Elite drawing-number patterns already used by Databook (e.g. `2025-033-1-2B`, `2026-075-1-1`). Do not invent a new scheme.
- After a send (future): Outlook from the real mailbox, Jira comment/transition, dated copy in the job folder.

## Always read

Before proposing or building, read `AGENTS.md` and `PROGRESS.md` in this workspace. Update `PROGRESS.md` when a decision is locked or a test is done.
